                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2020b1ec-35af-3712-8977-c93fd2a8adea",
                        "entry_id": "dde085df-e057-32d3-9d76-22e6d1484168",
                        "glosses": [
                            "разг., ирон. старая расхлябанная повозка, машина, велосипед и т. д."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "502f1c18-0efd-45d2-b8bb-cbd9a656cfc3",
                                "sense_id": "2020b1ec-35af-3712-8977-c93fd2a8adea",
                                "text": "— Если не торопитесь, помогите мне завести этот драндулет."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ca4404c-3c9f-4dd3-864d-5321f1a57573",
                                "sense_id": "2020b1ec-35af-3712-8977-c93fd2a8adea",
                                "text": "Я ехал на старом драндулете, у которого в каретке постоянно что-то щёлкало."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2de3164c-3aa4-34b1-825c-4312b45b391a",
                        "entry_id": "dde085df-e057-32d3-9d76-22e6d1484168",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар., разг. транспортное средство"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "33780627-7ddf-4041-986e-ac7c4f1ebd0a",
                                "sense_id": "2de3164c-3aa4-34b1-825c-4312b45b391a",
                                "text": "Пулемёты возили на лёгких бричках и драндулетах, запряжённых парами и четвёрками по большей части отличных лошадей."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9c6c58ed-21f5-342c-8682-fb7a461ef8dd",
                        "entry_id": "dde085df-e057-32d3-9d76-22e6d1484168",
                        "glosses": [
                            "ирон. механизм, агрегат неясного назначения"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "10362489-aae6-4563-8d8d-a34285ae72d0",
                                "sense_id": "9c6c58ed-21f5-342c-8682-fb7a461ef8dd",
                                "text": "Воистину вы играете на драндулете, а я на прямой кишке."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c1457d69-237b-4173-b15d-1d5f37d8b0b6",
                        "source_entry_id": "dde085df-e057-32d3-9d76-22e6d1484168",
                        "source_sense_description": "старая расхлябанная повозка, машина, велосипед и т. д.",
                        "target_lang_word": "jalopy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "jalopy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "208b09fb-49cd-3c8b-b657-a10b574f5d91",
                                        "entry_id": "fa980c29-f42e-3301-b30f-293ed92e07a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An old, dilapidated or unpretentious automobile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "213b1f58-957b-4fc9-9c69-a9ea51c3d321",
                                                "sense_id": "208b09fb-49cd-3c8b-b657-a10b574f5d91",
                                                "text": "Dean is the perfect guy for the road because he was actually born on the road, when his parents were passing through Salt Lake City in 1926, in a jalopy, on their way to Los Angeles."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c829b11-e3cf-478b-83d0-ffc3e67b10d2",
                                                "sense_id": "208b09fb-49cd-3c8b-b657-a10b574f5d91",
                                                "text": "\"We ran into some real excitement,\" Frank said, and told his father the whole story of Chet's missing jalopy, the wrecked car which they suspected had been a stolen one also, and the attempted holdup at the ferryboat office."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "48bd7974-f081-43e3-80b2-cb1d55491809",
                                                "sense_id": "208b09fb-49cd-3c8b-b657-a10b574f5d91",
                                                "text": "There's only a rough track and I doubt if that jalopy of yours will make it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae200572-f379-48e9-a83a-fc043a3ea7eb",
                                                "sense_id": "208b09fb-49cd-3c8b-b657-a10b574f5d91",
                                                "text": "Through most of those early years of restless travel, he dragged his two children and his long-suffering wife, Maryann[…] behind him like tin cans tied to the bumper of a jalopy that no car dealer in his right mind would take in trade."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "303cfd4e-91e3-3f79-94be-ec41d7e52292",
                                        "entry_id": "fa980c29-f42e-3301-b30f-293ed92e07a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hip, cool, groovy automobile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "US",
                                            "dated",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5f40848e-d18b-472a-92a6-2a11f9224cbc",
                        "source_entry_id": "dde085df-e057-32d3-9d76-22e6d1484168",
                        "source_sense_description": "старая расхлябанная повозка, машина, велосипед и т. д.",
                        "target_lang_word": "rattletrap",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rattletrap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fdeeb625-f1d4-3a4c-adb4-5e17b1bbf871",
                                        "entry_id": "8befcfd7-e144-3a6e-a810-6685bec4ba02",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Mechanically unreliable or in disrepair."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de0bfe4d-ec01-4e1a-94e5-b39e03cab765",
                                                "sense_id": "fdeeb625-f1d4-3a4c-adb4-5e17b1bbf871",
                                                "text": "2006, Paul McGeough, Bush 'palace' shielded from Iraqi storm, theage.com.au, August 26, http://www.theage.com.au/news/world/bush-palace-shielded-from-iraqi-storm/2006/08/25/1156012740594.html,\nAll services for the biggest embassy in the world will operate independently from the rattletrap utilities of the Iraqi capital. (speaking of the new US Embassy in Baghdad)"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2c04922f-243d-4ce3-90af-1bf95e5ba861",
                                                "sense_id": "fdeeb625-f1d4-3a4c-adb4-5e17b1bbf871",
                                                "text": "Every cultural instinct and previous experience tells you that when you travel this far you should find, at the very least, people on camels. There should be unrecognizable lettering on the signs, and swarthy men in robes drinking coffee from thimble-sized cups and puffing on hookahs, and rattletrap buses and potholes in the road and a real possibility of disease on everything you touch—but no, it's not like that at all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ab8c32f-bec2-4862-8fe3-7e9809bc9afe",
                                                "sense_id": "fdeeb625-f1d4-3a4c-adb4-5e17b1bbf871",
                                                "text": "BLANCHE:What you are talking about is brutal desire--just--Desire!--the name of that rattle-trap streetcar that bangs through the Quarter, up one old narrow street and down another..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "rattletrap",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7c349fc8-1c01-365c-b071-a11d17090a5e",
                                        "entry_id": "bf075cee-d577-389f-b6ef-8e440a9c99e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mechanical device, particularly an automobile, that is worn out, run down, or mechanically unreliable as indicated by noises it makes in operation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "417ebff0-0f9a-4476-9bc9-ead7368beb56",
                                                "sense_id": "7c349fc8-1c01-365c-b071-a11d17090a5e",
                                                "text": "Mom always worried about our safety in my friend's rattletrap. I told her not to worry, as it can't go fast enough to be dangerous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c64f379c-7be0-3ee0-afe5-380fbe4e684b",
                                        "entry_id": "bf075cee-d577-389f-b6ef-8e440a9c99e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any piece of miscellaneous equipment or junk."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ba76ee41-02a5-4868-9f5b-9b7b315c60f5",
                                                "sense_id": "c64f379c-7be0-3ee0-afe5-380fbe4e684b",
                                                "text": "And they tumbled about the rattletraps under the cupboard, and rummaged the drawers in search of the sacred volume."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0ac81f5a-0b3f-3baf-9e2c-33ee227a9e46",
                                        "entry_id": "bf075cee-d577-389f-b6ef-8e440a9c99e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A type of noisemaker in which the teeth of a gear repeatedly bend and release a stiff tongue."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acb4b583-0388-31a6-881c-790d5a38c20f",
                                        "entry_id": "bf075cee-d577-389f-b6ef-8e440a9c99e7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person's mouth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9f39410-4cfd-46e9-bf6c-4757f1fae993",
                                                "sense_id": "acb4b583-0388-31a6-881c-790d5a38c20f",
                                                "text": "Shut your rattletrap!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fc8af8df-188c-42ce-b616-fe1ccba43e47",
                        "source_entry_id": "dde085df-e057-32d3-9d76-22e6d1484168",
                        "source_sense_description": "старая расхлябанная повозка, машина, велосипед и т. д.",
                        "target_lang_word": "clunker",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "clunker",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9d57926-7fc4-3ae7-9f3a-b37c091fc1c4",
                                        "entry_id": "b942d8fc-b7e0-3c68-9e58-1f37edc9cc33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A decrepit motor car."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "850d071a-2179-48de-bc3c-91248931b75f",
                                                "sense_id": "c9d57926-7fc4-3ae7-9f3a-b37c091fc1c4",
                                                "text": "The only rig nobody'd recognize is that clunker that Vic drove here in, and he won't take it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0dd67f8e-0d84-40d3-bcf5-99cebde2968f",
                                                "sense_id": "c9d57926-7fc4-3ae7-9f3a-b37c091fc1c4",
                                                "text": "2008 July 9, Jacqueline Mitchell, “America's Most Stolen Vehicles”, in Forbes magazine,\nSo don't think for a moment that your old but tired vehicle matters only to you. Your clunker is cash money to professional thieves."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd568ef2-0b1c-36f6-9dfb-7875768eab86",
                                        "entry_id": "b942d8fc-b7e0-3c68-9e58-1f37edc9cc33",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Anything which is in poor condition or of poor quality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b2df3f1-781f-48e9-b742-ac60a1e28f81",
                                                "sense_id": "bd568ef2-0b1c-36f6-9dfb-7875768eab86",
                                                "text": "It seemed silly for the crowd to applaud or groan over what you had already felt in your fingers or even in your arms as you braced to shoot or for that matter in your eyes: when he was hot he could see the separate threads wound into the strings looping the hoop. Yet at the start of the game when you came out for warm-up and could see all the town clunkers sitting in the back of the bleachers elbowing each other and the cheerleaders wisecracking with the racier male teachers, the crowd then seemed right inside you, your liver and lungs and stomach."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5b677c6f-4ce3-45b0-a0ab-5c1f686ed937",
                                                "sense_id": "bd568ef2-0b1c-36f6-9dfb-7875768eab86",
                                                "text": "I bought an old clunker of a typewriter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4eea4af7-8239-4956-975c-024371258136",
                                                "sense_id": "bd568ef2-0b1c-36f6-9dfb-7875768eab86",
                                                "text": "All of the stories have a subtle undercurrent of brutality, and the writing is consistently sharp, direct and darkly funny, and there’s not a clunker in the bunch."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
